{
  "voice_id": "nPczCjzI2devNBz1zQrb",
  "text": "Every night, your body does five strange things, and you never notice a single one. One: it paralyzes you. During dream sleep, your brain shuts off almost every muscle, so you don't act out your dreams. Two: your brain takes a bath. Fluid washes through it, flushing out the waste that builds up while you're awake. Three: you grow taller. With no weight pressing down, the discs in your spine expand. You wake up about a centimeter taller. Four: your nose stops guarding you. Smell almost never wakes a sleeping person, which is exactly why you need a smoke alarm. Five: that sudden falling jolt? It's a hypnic jerk, your muscles twitching as you slip into sleep. So tonight, when you close your eyes, remember:",
